mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Professional internship refers to the practical teaching process in which students of pharmacy (including clinical pharmacy direction) are arranged to actual job positions in hospitals, drug regulatory authorities, pharmaceutical companies and other related enterprises in a planned, organized and guided manner in accordance with the training objectives and teaching plans of the pharmacy major. Through participating in practical activities such as drug research and development, production, circulation, application and management, students apply the theoretical knowledge they have learned to actual work to gain professional experience, cultivate professional abilities and improve their comprehensive qualities.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
